<title>FRANCE: ADP-Paris Jan-Feb 97 export traffic up 1.4pct.</title>
<headline>ADP-Paris Jan-Feb 97 export traffic up 1.4pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>86,579 tonnes of air cargo</p>
<p>exports left the</p>
<p>two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in</p>
<p>January-February 1997, up</p>
<p>1.4 percent on the same period last year , airport authority</p>
<p>figures show.</p>
<p>January-February 1997 export traffic from the Paris airports</p>
<p>by region,</p>
<p>with percentage change against the same period 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>			    Tonnes    Pct change on</p>
<p>					  Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p> Domestic		  6,826    down  7.1pct</p>
<p> European Union	 10,847    up   11.0</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	   1,943    up    7.1</p>
<p> North Africa	    1,563    down  7.7</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    7,101    up    3.9</p>
<p> North America	  23,302    up    4.4</p>
<p> French territories    4,076    down  4.1</p>
<p> Latin America	   4,890    up   11.7</p>
<p> Middle East	     8,316    up    1.5</p>
<p> Far East		 17,715    down  5.5</p>
<p> Total		    86,579     up   1.4</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
